  </bp:Protein>
  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference16">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P31040 SDHA</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SDHA</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SDH2</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SDHF</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref227" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Flavoprotein (FP) subunit of succinate dehydrogenase (SDH) that is involved in complex II of the mitochondrial electron transport chain and is responsible for transferring electrons from succinate to ubiquinone (coenzyme Q) (PubMed:10746566, PubMed:24781757). SDH also oxidizes malate to the non-canonical enol form of oxaloacetate, enol-oxaloacetate (By similarity). Enol-oxaloacetate, which is a potent inhibitor of the succinate dehydrogenase activity, is further isomerized into keto-oxaloacetate (By similarity). Can act as a tumor suppressor (PubMed:20484225).CATALYTIC ACTIVITY a ubiquinone + succinate = a ubiquinol + fumarateCATALYTIC ACTIVITY (R)-malate + a quinone = enol-oxaloacetate + a quinolCATALYTIC ACTIVITY (S)-malate + a quinone = enol-oxaloacetate + a quinolCOFACTOR Enol-oxaloacetate inhibits the succinate dehydrogenase activity.PATHWAY Carbohydrate metabolism; tricarboxylic acid cycle; fumarate from succinate (eukaryal route): step 1/1.SUBUNIT Component of complex II composed of four subunits: the flavoprotein (FP) SDHA, iron-sulfur protein (IP) SDHB, and a cytochrome b560 composed of SDHC and SDHD (PubMed:37098072). Interacts with SDHAF2/SDH5; interaction is required for FAD attachment (PubMed:19628817, PubMed:32887801). Interacts with TRAP1 (PubMed:23747254). Interacts with LACC1 (PubMed:28593945).INTERACTION Phosphorylation at Tyr-215 is important for efficient electron transfer in complex II and the prevention of ROS generation.PTM Acetylated. Deacetylated by SIRT3.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the FAD-dependent oxidoreductase 2 family. FRD/SDH subfamily.SEQUENCE CAUTION Extended N-terminus.SEQUENCE CAUTION Differs extensively from that shown.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
