  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference21">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P40926 MDH2</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MDH2</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref268" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CATALYTIC ACTIVITY (S)-malate + NAD(+) = oxaloacetate + NADH + H(+)ACTIVITY REGULATION Enzyme activity is enhanced by acetylation.SUBUNIT Homodimer.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Acetylation is enhanced by up to 67% after treatment either with trichostin A (TSA) or with nicotinamide (NAM) with the appearance of tri- and tetraacetylations. Glucose also increases acetylation by about 60%.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the LDH/MDH superfamily. MDH type 1 family.ONLINE INFORMATION Malate dehydrogenase entry</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
