    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref363" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref364" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NAD-dependent protein deacetylase sirtuin-3 (SIRT-3) deacetylates lysine-413 residue of IDH2, restoring its enzymatic activity. Since IDH2 is the main producer of NADPH, SIRT3 has a direct effect on the antioxidant level in mitochondria (Lombard et al., 2007; Yu et al., 2012; Chen et al., 2021; reviewed in Gao &amp; Shen, 2023).</bp:comment>
