  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference28">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q86U28 ISCA2</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ISCA2</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HBLD1</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref381" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Involved in the maturation of mitochondrial 4Fe-4S proteins functioning late in the iron-sulfur cluster assembly pathway. May be involved in the binding of an intermediate of Fe/S cluster assembly.SUBUNIT Heterotetramer; forms a dimer of dimers with IBA57 (PubMed:31831856). Interacts with [2Fe-2S]-ISCA2 forming the heterodimer [2Fe- 2S]-ISCA2-IBA57 complex; [2Fe-2S] cluster binding is absolutely required to promote the complex formation (PubMed:30269484).INTERACTION The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the HesB/IscA family.SEQUENCE CAUTION Extended N-terminus.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
