    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q9BUE6 ISCA1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ISCA1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HBLD2</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GK004</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref384" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Involved in the maturation of mitochondrial 4Fe-4S proteins functioning late in the iron-sulfur cluster assembly pathway. Probably involved in the binding of an intermediate of Fe/S cluster assembly.SUBUNIT Interacts with CRY2, but not with CRY1 (in vitro).INTERACTION Detected in cerebellum, kidney and heart.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the HesB/IscA family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
