    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref432" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After translation in cytosol and translocation to the mitochondrial inner membrane SDH subunits C and D (SDHC, SDHD), together with the heme b cofactor, bind to the assembled cytosolic SDHA:SDHB construct to form the fully functional SDH complex. Although a full structure of the porcine complex exists (PDB 1ZOY) no details are known about the last steps of the assembly. However, successful assembly depends on the presence of both the SDHC heme b cofactor and the C-terminal tail of the SDHA subunit. (Lemarie &amp; Grimm, 2009; Kim et al., 2012; reviewed in Van Vranken et al., 2014; Signes &amp; Fernandez-Vizarra, 2018).</bp:comment>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref90" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref94" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref95" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref92" />
    <bp:dataSource rdf:resource="#Provenance1" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Authored: Stephan, Ralf, 2023-11-29</bp:comment>
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reviewed: Hill, David P, 2024-02-15</bp:comment>
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Edited: D'Eustachio, Peter, 2024-02-15</bp:comment>
  </bp:BiochemicalReaction>
